WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.054 --> 00:00:04.945
Ally stared at the spot in the trees where her pod should be.

2
00:00:04.946 --> 00:00:09.229
"It can't be gone!" she thought. "It has to be here somewhere."

3
00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:13.231
"Alpha!" Ally cried. "Where are you?"

4
00:00:13.232 --> 00:00:15.908
There was no answer.

5
00:00:15.909 --> 00:00:24.443
Ally spent the next thirty minutes looking high and low for the pod.

6
00:00:24.444 --> 00:00:29.956
She'd been trying not to think the worst, but she couldn't hold the thought off any longer.

7
00:00:29.957 --> 00:00:33.455
"Dr. Lloyd's machine finally worked," she thought.

8
00:00:33.456 --> 00:00:47.386
"He found my pod. And if he can find my pod, it won't be long before he finds me!"

9
00:00:47.387 --> 00:00:51.864
Ally was close to tears as she sat down on a park bench.

10
00:00:51.865 --> 00:00:57.000
With her pod gone, there was no hope she'd ever get back home.

11
00:00:57.001 --> 00:01:00.821
But even worse, she'd lost a friend—Alpha.

12
00:01:00.822 --> 00:01:05.347
Ally replayed their last morning together in her mind.

13
00:01:05.348 --> 00:01:10.178
That's when she realized what had happened: she’d forgotten to camouflage the pod!

14
00:01:10.179 --> 00:01:16.456
"Oh no!" she moaned, burying her head in her hands.

15
00:01:16.457 --> 00:01:22.811
"My parents were right about me. I am totally irresponsible!"

16
00:01:22.812 --> 00:01:28.345
"Ally?" Mateo rode up on his bicycle. "What's wrong?"

17
00:01:28.346 --> 00:01:32.935
"It's all my fault, Mateo!" Ally moaned.

18
00:01:32.936 --> 00:01:36.097
"What's your fault?" Ally heard a girl say. It

19
00:01:36.098 --> 00:01:39.844
was Bethany's voice, but Ally didn't see her. Mateo

20
00:01:39.845 --> 00:01:44.542
held up his phone—Bethany was on speakerphone. Ally

21
00:01:44.543 --> 00:01:49.624
shook her head, to show Mateo she couldn't talk about it with Bethany. "Not

22
00:01:49.625 --> 00:01:52.428
fault ," Mateo said quickly.

23
00:01:52.429 --> 00:01:58.297
"Ally told me to halt . She was joking. I'll, uh, call you

24
00:01:58.298 --> 00:02:02.866
later." "Oh, okay. I—," Bethany began as Mateo hung

25
00:02:02.867 --> 00:02:08.771
up. "What happened, Ally?" he asked. "You look like you’ve lost your best

26
00:02:08.772 --> 00:02:12.879
friend." "I did." Ally

27
00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:22.108
sighed. "Alpha warned me not to forget to camouflage the pod when we left, but I was so busy trying to make you laugh, I totally

28
00:02:22.109 --> 00:02:25.604
forgot!" "I don't understand. What happened to

29
00:02:25.605 --> 00:02:28.124
Alpha?" "It's not just Alpha!" Ally

30
00:02:28.125 --> 00:02:35.702
said. "It's the entire pod. I forgot to camouflage it after we left, and Dr. Lloyd must have found

31
00:02:35.703 --> 00:02:43.755
it! What am I going to do? How am I going to ever get back home, and where am I going to sleep until

32
00:02:43.756 --> 00:02:48.256
then?" "Whoa, whoa." Mateo gestured for Ally to slow

33
00:02:48.257 --> 00:02:56.133
down. "One problem at a time. Maybe someone moved the pod. Let's not jump to

34
00:02:56.134 --> 00:03:00.808
conclusions." "I'm not jumping anywhere." Ally

35
00:03:00.809 --> 00:03:09.087
sniffled. "I meant, we won't know what happened until we look. Come on. Let's search some

36
00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:20.683
more." Ally and Mateo walked through the entire park, but the pod was nowhere to be

37
00:03:20.684 --> 00:03:24.551
found. "Dr. Lloyd has it." Ally

38
00:03:24.552 --> 00:03:27.564
sighed. "He said he was certain he'd lured a ship to

39
00:03:27.565 --> 00:03:33.447
Earth. He probably took it to the UFO museum, but I can't risk going there to look for

40
00:03:33.448 --> 00:03:37.849
it." "Don't worry," Mateo said. "I'll go there first thing in the

41
00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:45.373
morning. We'll find your pod and Alpha. I promise. And until then you'll stay with Papi and

42
00:03:45.374 --> 00:03:57.929
me." "That's so nice of you." Ally blew her

43
00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:01.888
nose. "But what if your dad finds out I'm an

44
00:04:01.889 --> 00:04:09.571
Astralian?" "You'll just have to be careful to take off your meld medallion only at night, after Papi has gone to

45
00:04:09.572 --> 00:04:12.946
bed." "You don't think he'll mind having me

46
00:04:12.947 --> 00:04:17.233
stay?" "Of course not." Mateo pulled out his

47
00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:19.995
phone. "Hi, Papi. We need a

48
00:04:19.996 --> 00:04:23.029
favor." "Whatever you need, son," Ray

49
00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:26.896
said. "Ally needs to stay with us for a while. You see, her place went—"

50
